    ["Subtracting the smaller digit from the larger in each column regardless of position (542 - 267 = 325).", "Forgetting to reduce the column you traded from.", "Rounding and then adjusting the wrong way.", "Not checking by adding.", "Treating a zero in the next column as if it could give a ten."],
    [{"title": "Change Maker", "description": "Pretend to run a shop. Choose five prices under $100 and work out the change from $100 by counting on. Write each count.", "type": "create", "difficulty": "medium", "evidence_type": "photo"}],
    "Part A: 4, 3, 6, 35. Part B: 44, 64, 34, 353. Part C: 47, 55, 34, 146. Part D: 275, 273, 238. Part E (suggested): 91 - 88 count on = 3; 84 - 52 partition = 32; 83 - 29 round and adjust = 54; 702 - 345 columns = 357. Part F: any correct adding check, for example 275 + 267 = 542.",
